   "claims": [
    "Answer shows the work to convert to cubic yards: Divide cubic feet by 27.",
    "How to Convert Cubic Feet to Cubic Yards Divide cubic feet by 27 Explanation One yard is 3 feet long.",
    "Cubing both values, 1 yard cubed equals 27 feet cubed.",
    "1 yd = 3 ft (1 yd)³ = (3 ft)³ 1 yd × 1 yd × 1 yd = 3 ft × 3 ft × 3 ft 1 yd³ = 27 ft³ So there are 27 cubic feet per cubic yard.",
    "To convert, take any number of cubic feet and divide by 27 to get cubic yards.",
    "yd³ = ft³ ÷ 27 Visualize Cubic Feet in a Cubic Yard You can think of a cubic yard of volume as a box that measures one yard tall, by one yard wide, by one yard deep.",
    "Within this space there are 27 cubic feet, which are cubes measuring one ft wide by one ft tall by one ft deep.",
    "This image shows how cubic feet are arranged within a cubic yard, stacked in rows and columns 3 feet high by 3 feet wide and 3 feet deep.",
    "So another way to convert cubic feet to cubic yards is to multiply cubic feet by the inverse of 27.",
    "Inverse of 27 = 1/27 1 ÷ 27 = 0.037037 cubic feet × 0.037037 = cubic yards So you can multiply cubic feet by 0.037037 to get cubic yards."
   ],
